special_abilities:
  - name: "Magic Tattoos (Marks of Heritage)"
    description: "Every True Atlantean bears a heart impaled by a wooden stake (no blood) on the right wrist, for protection from vampires, and a flaming sword on the left wrist that creates a magic M.D.C. weapon; a clan crest may form the sword''s hilt. Placed at age five or six. They are two of the Undead Slayer''s 18 starting tattoos and follow the standard tattoo rules."
  - name: "Magic Tattoos"
    description: "A typical first level Undead Slayer starts with 18 tattoos: the flaming sword (an M.D. weapon that hurts vampires); a bow and arrow or crossbow whose four arrows are flaming (M.D.) and winged (triple range, magically return); the powers protection from vampires (heart impaled by a stake), turn dead (the cross), invulnerability (heart in chains), control the forces of air (cloud in chains), basic healing (rose), super healing (Phoenix) and knowledge and reading (eye); plus two powers, two simple weapons, two magic weapons, two animals and one monster of choice. Simple weapons, animals and monsters are one row each (All Simple Weapons, Animals, Monsters), so the specific weapons, beasts and monster are recorded here. Each level a clan elder or clan alchemist adds two simple tattoos (animal or simple weapon) or one major tattoo (power, monster or magic weapon); this may mean a trip to another dimension and a delay. Never more than two tattoos at one time, and at least six months between pairs."
  - name: "Increased P.P.E. from Magic Tattoos"
    description: "Base P.P.E. is 2D4x10 for all Undead Slayers, male and female, plus 10 per level of experience and six for each tattoo. The 18 starting tattoos (+108) and first level (+10) are the +118 in ppe_base; add six for every tattoo gained later. The book puts a typical first level Undead Slayer at about 162 to 222 P.P.E. Can also draw energy from ley lines and nexus points."
  - name: "Increased P.P.E. Recovery"
    description: "Recovers 20 P.P.E. per hour of rest or sleep, four times the normal human rate."
  - name: "M.D.C. Transformation"
    description: "Base M.D.C. 2D4x10, plus 11 M.D.C. (male) or 13 M.D.C. (female) for each tattoo beyond six. The male and female variants apply this for the 18 starting tattoos (12 beyond six); add 11 or 13 for each tattoo gained later."
  - name: "Cannot Be Physically Transformed"
    description: "Immune to metamorphosis potions and spells, the transformation ritual, vampire transformation, petrification, turn to mist, growth or shrinking by spell or potion, and any other magic or supernatural transformation spell, curse, wish or enchantment."
  - name: "Continued Growth"
    description: "After adulthood at about age 25, True Atlanteans grow about an inch a century, for an average adult height of 6 ft 6 in to about 7 ft (1.95 to 2.1 m)."
  - name: "Sense Vampires"
    description: "Senses vampires and vampire intelligences within 1000 ft (305 m) without pinpointing the source. Recognizes a vampire by appearance: 12% per level of experience."
  - name: "Operate Dimensional Pyramids"
    description: "Knows how to operate the stone masters'' pyramids for communication and dimensional teleportation. Base skill 40% +5% per level of experience. Does not know how stone magic works or how to build pyramids."
  - name: "Sense Ley Lines"
    description: "Same as the Line Walker."
  - name: "Sense Rifts"
    description: "Same as the Line Walker."
  - name: "Ley Line Phasing"
    description: "Same as the Line Walker (Rifts, page 83)."
  - name: "Supernatural Being"
    description: "Undead Slayers are considered supernatural beings."
restrictions:
  - "Always a True Atlantean."
  - "Should start at first or second level of experience."
  - "Cybernetics: none. Bio-systems only if ever needed; even one mechanical arm or leg reduces the effects, range, damage and duration of the character''s magic by 25%."
  - "No more than two new tattoos at one time, and at least six months between pairs."
side_effects: "Insanity: none at the start of the O.C.C., other than an almost obsessive commitment to help others and fight evil. Vampires and the Minions of Splugorth are hated above all."
extraction_notes: "WB2 printed 97-99 (cache p097-p099, page_offset 0): the O.C.C. begins on printed 97 after the Maxi-Man, runs through 98 and ends on 99 before Stone Magic & The Stone Masters; its introduction is on printed 17 (the Quick Find cites 17 & 97). Printed 98 (skills under a full-width illustration, OCR scrambled) was rendered and read off the image. || XP: the Undead Slayers ladder on printed 68, rendered and read off the image: lower bounds 0, 2501, 5501, 10501, 21501, 32001, 47001, 65001, 87001, 115001, 170001, 220001, 300001, 400001, 500001. atlantean-monster-hunter borrows it. || GROUP: the book files no group heading. Stored as men-of-arms: a tattooed warrior, not a spell caster by training. mdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line. || RACE: always a True Atlantean. Following atlantean-monster-hunter, race_restrictions is only none and the True Atlantean racial block (printed 16) is recorded in the True Atlanteans section; the O.C.C.''s own Atlantean characteristics (printed 97-98) supersede the racial ones where they differ (recognize vampires 12% per level, pyramids 40%+5%, save and attribute bonuses). horror_factor 14 is the racial block''s figure for an Undead Slayer. || POOLS: M.D.C. 2D4x10 plus 11 (male) or 13 (female) per tattoo beyond six; all 18 starting tattoos count (they include the two Marks of Heritage, which the book calls two of the 18 to 50), so 12 beyond six: 2d4x10+132 and 2d4x10+156. P.P.E. 2D4x10 plus six per tattoo (108) plus 10 per level. The book''s own example, 162 to 222 at first level, is 24 higher than that arithmetic gives (138 to 198); stored as the formula, the example kept in prose. No hit points or S.D.C. stored, following atlantean-monster-hunter. || BONUSES: +4 save vs magic of all kinds (spell_magic and ritual_magic), +8 save vs horror factor, +2 M.E., +2 P.E., +2 P.S., +6 Spd, unconditional. || TATTOOS are catalog spells, tradition tattoo. The flaming sword is Weapon Covered in Flames; the flaming, winged bow or crossbow adds Weapon with Wings (a weapon may carry more than one feature, printed 87); the seven fixed powers map by image to Heart Pierced by a Wooden Stake, Cross, Heart Encircled by Chains, Chain Wrapped Around a Cloud, Rose and Thorny Stem, Phoenix Rising From the Flames (the index on printed 91 lists Healing: Super and Resurrection under the Phoenix) and Eye of Knowledge. All Simple Weapons, Animals and Monsters are granted once each and the counts are prose. The level-up grant is one major tattoo per level from 2 to 15; the alternative of two simple tattoos adds no row and is prose. || SKILLS: Radio: Basic 45+10; Dragonese/Elf, American and Greek at 98% mapped as atlantean-monster-hunter does (Language: Dragonese, Literacy: Dragonese/Elven, Language: Native Tongue, Literacy: Native Language, Language: Ancient Greek at 98, and a Literacy: Other pick at 98 for Greek); three languages of choice +15% as three Language: Other picks. Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic 45+20; Intelligence 32+10; Tracking is Tracking (people) 25+15; Wilderness Survival 30+15; Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+25; Lore: Faerie is Lore: Faeries & Creatures of Magic 25+10; Gymnastics and Swimming +5; W.P. Archery & Targeting is W.P. Archery. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts with no price printed, so no hand_to_hand block. || RELATED: four, plus three additional skills at levels four, eight and twelve, read as one at each (three in all), as atlantean-monster-hunter reads the same sentence; three at each is the alternative. Pilot except robot and power armor excludes Robots & Power Armor and every Robot Combat row; Technical except computer. || MONEY: 4D6x1000 in precious gems or artifacts, which are salable goods rather than coin; starting_money omitted and the figure kept in prose. || EQUIPMENT: the unnamed high-powered energy rifle and energy pistol are choices from the catalog''s common sets; 1D4 silver-plated knives, a wooden cross, a dozen wooden stakes and a mallet are stored. The 1D4 techno-wizard anti-vampire weapons (storm flares, globe of daylight flares, TW water shotgun; Rifts Vampire Kingdoms 31-32) have no catalog rows and are prose; no stubs were made for another book''s gear."
---

## Lore

The True Atlanteans have raised an elite order of warriors sworn to wipe out supernatural evil. Like knights-errant they travel from world to world and dimension to dimension, protecting the innocent, destroying monsters and freeing those enslaved by vampires and their kind. Vampires, vampire intelligences and the Minions of Splugorth are their archenemies. They are the Undead Slayers, a True Atlantean tattooed warrior order empowered by tattoo magic. All True Atlanteans carry two to six tattoos without being counted as Tattooed Men; the Undead Slayer is the one Atlantean who becomes a full Tattooed Man, covered in 18 to 50 tattoos.

Earth''s place in history as the Atlantean homeland, and the adventure waiting there, has drawn many young Atlanteans to it, and for many it is their first time in combat.

Standard equipment is typically a high-powered energy rifle and energy pistol, 1D4 silver-plated knives, a wooden cross, a dozen wooden stakes and a mallet, and likely 1D4 kinds of techno-wizard anti-vampire weapons, such as storm flares, globe of daylight flares and the TW water shotgun (Rifts Vampire Kingdoms). Money is 4D6x1000 in precious gems or artifacts, though Undead Slayers care little for wealth and tend to spend what they gather helping or protecting others.

## Magic Tattoos

A first level Undead Slayer starts with 18 tattoos, including the flaming sword, a flaming winged bow or crossbow, and seven fixed powers: protection from vampires, turn dead, invulnerability, control of the forces of air, basic healing, super healing and knowledge and reading. The rest are two powers, two simple weapons, two magic weapons, two animals and one monster of choice. Each new level a clan elder or alchemist adds two simple tattoos or one major one, which may mean a few days'' journey to another dimension.

## True Atlanteans

The racial block the book prints for all True Atlanteans (printed 16), for an Undead Slayer played with no R.C.C.:

- Alignment: any, most principled, scrupulous or unprincipled.
- Attributes: I.Q. 3D6+4, M.E. 4D6+6, M.A. 3D6+4, P.S. 4D6+4, P.P. 3D6, P.E. 3D6+6, P.B. 3D6+6, Spd 4D6+6.
- Hit Points: P.E. +1D6 per level. S.D.C.: 50 plus O.C.C., tattoo and physical skill S.D.C. Only Undead Slayers and Tattooed Men are mega-damage creatures.
- Horror Factor: 14 for an Undead Slayer, 12 for the average Atlantean.
- Height 6 ft plus 1D4 inches, plus an inch per century of age; weight 170 lbs and up. Appear 19 to 35 while anywhere from 19 to 250 years old; the average life span is 500 years.
- Appearance entirely human: tall, handsome, dark-haired. Typically bold, headstrong loners, but kind, merciful, noble, honest and brave.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'undead-slayer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'undead-slayer';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-undead-slayer-class.sql');
